('CIT_WEL_PRYDERI_MABINO','ENT_WEL_PRYDERI','SRC_MABINOGION','The Mabinogion','The Mabinogion','MATH THE SON OF MATHONWY THIS IS THE FOURTH PORTION OF THE MABINOGI Math the son of Mathonwy was lord over Gwynedd, and Pryderi the son of Pwyll was lord over the one-and-twenty Cantrevs of the South; and these were the seven Cantrevs of Dyved, and the seven Cantrevs of Morganwc, the four Cantrevs of Ceredigiawn, and the three of Ystrad Tywi.','Lady Charlotte Guest',1877,'https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/5160',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'English translation located by name within the work; verify locus.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_WEL_PWYLL_MABINO','ENT_WEL_PWYLL','SRC_MABINOGION','The Mabinogion','The Mabinogion','And by reason of his having dwelt that year in Annwvyn, and having ruled there so prosperously, and united the two kingdoms in one day by his valour and prowess, he lost the name of Pwyll Prince of Dyved, and was called Pwyll Chief of Annwvyn from that time forward. * * * * * Once upon a time, Pwyll was at Narberth his chief palace, where a feast had been prepared for him, and with him was a great host of men.','Lady Charlotte Guest',1877,'https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/5160',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'English translation located by name within the work; verify locus.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_WEL_RHIANNON_MABINO','ENT_WEL_RHIANNON','SRC_MABINOGION','The Mabinogion','The Mabinogion','Pwyll, also, the Chief of Annwvyn, came to the orchard with his hundred knights, as Rhiannon had commanded him, having the bag with him. And Pwyll was clad in coarse and ragged garments, and wore large clumsy old shoes upon his feet. And when he knew that the carousal after the meat had begun, he went towards the hall, and when he came into the hall, he saluted Gwawl the son of Clud, and his company, both men and women.','Lady Charlotte Guest',1877,'https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/5160',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'English translation located by name within the work; verify locus.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1)
